    70	def rot_suffix(rotate_deg):
    71	    """The injective filename suffix for a yaw offset: ``5.625 -> '_rot5p625'``.
    72	
    73	    Integer rotations keep their historical byte-identical form (exp_02's
    74	    ``_rot180`` artifacts must still resolve); fractional ones would collide
    75	    under ``int()`` -- R3 evaluates 5.625 deg, which used to land on ``_rot5``
    76	    alongside 5 deg -- so they get a decimal-safe form (round-4 review B3).
    77	
    78	    Exposed as its own function because the R3 EVAL NAME needs the same
    79	    rendering as the filename: five rotation rows of one cell otherwise share an
    80	    eval name, and the identity that distinguishes them lives only in a field.
    81	    """
    82	    return '' if float(rotate_deg) == 0.0 else '_rot' + rot_token(rotate_deg)
